      "output": "## Review record: static source review, not actually run\n\nThe page was not opened in a browser and the simulation was never executed. Every finding comes from reading the HTML and JS. Determinism, the 0→13 flow, buffer limits and visual behaviour at run time are all unverified.\n\n### Confirmed (source reading)\n- **Flow 0→13:** `mv` moves a car only to `i+1`, or via `wbs`→5 and `pbs`→8. Stations are scanned 13→0, so a car advances at most one station per tick.\n- **Buffers:** `B.wbs.length<6` and `B.pbs.length<6` guard every push. Otherwise the car stays at 4 or 7 as blocked.\n- **Rework:** 4% at 7 goes to `rp`, then back to 6. 3% at 12 goes to `rq` with `w:90`, then back to 11.\n- **Yard:** at 24 cars, `splice(0,12)` ships 12.\n- **Faults:** `injectFault` sets `down` to 120 s. A down station blocks entry (`!S[i+1].down`), so the jam propagates upstream.\n- **Metrics:**\n  - JPH counts roll-offs in the last 3600 s.\n  - FTT is `ok/out`.\n  - WIP excludes yard and shipped cars.\n  - The sparkline adds a point every 300 s.\n- **Car look:** `lv`/`look` match the spec for stages 0–1, 2–4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10 and 11.\n- **State colours:** ring and HUD colours match the five-colour code.\n- **Controls:** pause and 1×/4×/16× use `15*speed` sim-seconds per 250 ms.\n- **Details panels:** car and station details exist.\n- **Label:** a red \"Simulated data\" pill is shown, and the page title says the same.\n- **External requests:** the only one is the cdnjs three.js r128 script. There is no fetch or XHR.\n\n### Defects\n1. **OEE:** `M.oee=u/13*M.ftt` is average utilisation × FTT. It is not availability × performance × quality.\n2. **Bottleneck:** `st=S.find(x=>x.down>0);if(st)b=st.id` reports the first down station as the bottleneck. Otherwise it uses cumulative `run/s.t` since t=0, which reacts slowly.\n3. **\"Cars done\" count:** the counter is `o.n++` inside `put`, so it counts entries, including the current car. It stays 0 at station 13.\n4. **Fault target:** `fault()` uses the stale `selSt`. After clicking a car, the fault hits the previously selected station.\n5. **AGVs ignore pause:** `agv.forEach(a=>{a.d=(a.d+2.5*dt)...})` keeps running while paused. The AGVs are also purely decorative and not linked to station 9.\n6. **Body-in-white look:** at stages 2–4, a dark chassis plate (`o.ch.visible=!sh`) is shown under the body-in-white.\n7. **Speed labels:** \"1×\" means 60 sim-s per real second, which is not real time, and the label does not say so.\n\n### Unverified (requires execution)\n- Rendering, shadows and the diorama look.\n- Click picking on cars and stations.\n- Point-sprite size under the orthographic camera.\n- Vehicle animation keeping up at 16×.\n- Float accumulation reaching `progress>.99999` exactly at the cycle time.\n- The CDN script actually loading.\n- Realistic JPH and OEE values.\n- Visible upstream jam rippling."
